{"candidate_id":"figure-analysis:Figure10:a84270a75b3eeacd","artifact_id":"Figure10","visual_type":"plot","description":"Two-panel line plot comparing CA (DeepCCA) and CA (VICReg) linear probe accuracy across nuisance alignment levels for dSprites and Shape3D, with separate panels for 10k and 100k pretraining samples and shaded variability bands for weak noise standard deviations 0.2, 0.5, and 0.9.","components":[{"name":"dSprites panel","role":"left subplot","visual_evidence":"Labeled '(a) dSprites' and headed 'Pretrain Samples: 10k'; x-axis shows nuisance alignment and y-axis shows linear probe accuracy."},{"name":"Shape3D panel","role":"right subplot","visual_evidence":"Labeled '(b) Shape3D' and headed 'Pretrain Samples: 100k'; x-axis shows nuisance alignment and y-axis shows linear probe accuracy."},{"name":"CA (DeepCCA)","role":"circular-marker method series","visual_evidence":"Legend identifies CA (DeepCCA) with dashed lines and circular markers."},{"name":"CA (VICReg)","role":"square-marker method series","visual_evidence":"Legend identifies CA (VICReg) with solid lines and square markers."},{"name":"Weak noise std 0.2","role":"condition series","visual_evidence":"Legend shows the dark purple condition labeled 0.2."},{"name":"Weak noise std 0.5","role":"condition series","visual_evidence":"Legend shows the blue condition labeled 0.5."},{"name":"Weak noise std 0.9","role":"condition series","visual_evidence":"Legend shows the teal condition labeled 0.9."}],"relationships":[{"source_component":"CA (DeepCCA)","relation":"is compared with","target_component":"CA (VICReg)"},{"source_component":"Weak noise std 0.2","relation":"defines a plotted condition for","target_component":"dSprites panel"},{"source_component":"Weak noise std 0.5","relation":"defines a plotted condition for","target_component":"Shape3D panel"},{"source_component":"Weak noise std 0.9","relation":"defines a plotted condition for","target_component":"dSprites panel"}],"findings":["The figure contains two subplots: dSprites on the left and Shape3D on the right.","The dSprites panel uses 10k pretraining samples, while the Shape3D panel uses 100k pretraining samples.","Both panels plot linear probe accuracy against nuisance alignment, with values spanning approximately 0.5 to 1.0 on the x-axis and 0.0 to 1.0 on the y-axis.","In dSprites, accuracy generally rises toward nuisance alignment around 0.8 and then drops near alignment 1.0 for both methods and noise conditions.","In Shape3D, the curves show more varied behavior around alignment 0.8 and converge near approximately 0.3–0.45 at alignment 1.0.","Shaded bands indicate variability around the plotted curves."],"citations":[{"section_id":"sec-1~23","path_id":"1~23","quote":"10Figure 10: Comparison between VICReg and DeepCCA for dSprites and Shape3D experiments"}],"confidence":0.96,"provenance":{"image_sha256":"dc83fa2e05268aa1eb695132c0f6ac9a44d5cf91dc69f80c6632954de9d594e8","context_sha256":"b7eeed66df39525a670ead248d79250a425c52bd8b0ecb85c6dbc1a3ee336a31","route_id":"figure-qa-luna","protocol":"openai_chat_completions","requested_model":"cx/gpt-5.6-luna","resolved_model":"cx/gpt-5.6-luna","prompt_sha256":"4786e6f3681b05b0e475e188f0fbd61e98def58906b98ae8010b07dfd44df596","output_schema_sha256":"0386bc6702386f87d7595f5a50c63b60d2fa20f22b58ef050ea6677616e6d1d8","schema_id":"chart_extraction","stage1_visual_type":"plot","prompt_task_sha256":"1dd7985b1567eda8d66c3da3478eab188eb6764f7e1445eb1b1014b72ad08dd6","route_policy_sha256":"897498afc82f7598dc9ebd6687dba16a821e18722262df3e299e45136eed1940","model_binding_sha256":"01208a249b295331443fdc61a0e35c1fe80cfdaea164f7a8d95c94b82517f43c","input_sha256":"0d292109a21c1c8df6017ef7e0ebfc9ae7b1aa94f2ed22edc10733d710c394ff","output_sha256":"fe0463ae06f24c28dc31973c4b93824ace00b73a4e9b2f07a6f8c3d0818cd75f","input_tokens":2612,"output_tokens":677,"latency_ms":14232},"typed_payload":null,"authoritative":false,"import_eligible":false}